course: dictionary
lesson: 14530
title: Perpetually: all the time, again and again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Perpetually» means all the time, without stopping. When you meet it, look at the sentence for clues: is something happening over and over, or never stopping? «My little brother is perpetually hungry.» He is not hungry just once. He is hungry again and again, and it seems never to stop.
explain: Try swapping in a word you know. «My little brother is always hungry» still makes sense, so perpetually means something close to always. The second meaning is "again and again, so often it seems constant": «Our neighbour is perpetually late for work.» He is late every time, so the sentence is about a habit that keeps happening.
explain: Perpetually is a formal, bookish word. You will meet it in stories, reports and science more than in everyday talk. In science it can describe something that never stops, like «the Earth perpetually spinning». Everyday speakers usually say always or all the time instead.
fact: Perpetually is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens.
fact: Perpetually means all the time, without stopping; forever.
fact: Perpetually can also mean again and again, so often that it seems constant.
fact: «Perpetually late» means late every time; «perpetually busy» means busy all the time.
fact: In everyday speech, people usually say «always» or «all the time» instead of perpetually.
exercise: «The cat was perpetually hungry.» What does perpetually mean here? | Only once in a while | Very quietly | Shortly before dinner | *All the time, without stopping
exercise: «He is perpetually late, so he always runs for the bus.» What does perpetually show? | That he is early for school every day | That he never catches the bus | *That he is late again and again | That he likes running in the rain
exercise: Find the word that means nearly the same as perpetually. | quietly | sometimes | *always | rarely
test: «The Earth is perpetually spinning.» Which meaning fits best in this sentence? | *Never stopping | Sitting still in one place | Stopping and starting again | Spinning only in the summer
test: Which everyday word could replace perpetually in «She is perpetually busy»? | *Always | Slowly | Rarely | Quietly
exam: Ella says, «Our dog is perpetually barking.» Which sentence has the same meaning? | Our dog barks once a year | Our dog never makes a sound | *Our dog is always barking | Our dog is barking in the garden only
